          %h1#apartness_spaces Apartness spaces
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#pointset_apartness_spaces"} Point–set apartness spaces
              %li
                %a{:href => "#separation_properties"} Separation properties
              %li
                %a{:href => "#relation_to_topological_spaces"} Relation to topological spaces
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %em apartness space
            is a set equipped with an “apartness relation” that distinguishes between pairs of points or sets. They are particularly interesting in
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            they tend to be equivalent to better-known definitions expressed in terms of “closeness” rather than “apartness”.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p There are actually several different notions of “apartness space” depending on whether the objects being compared on each side are points or sets.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %em point–point apartness space
                is a set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                equipped with an
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/apartness+relation"} apartness relation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo #
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x # y
                on elements
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y\in X
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tight+relation"} tight
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inequality+relation"} inequality relation
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong point–set apartness space
                is a set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                equipped with a relation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⋈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \bowtie A
                between points
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
                and subsets
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\subseteq X
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contrapositive"} contraposition
                from the definition of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                in terms of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} right exact
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+closure"} Moore closure
                operator, so that point–set apartness spaces are equivalent to topological spaces. In
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
                … well, keep reading.
            %li
              %p
                A
                %em set–set apartness space
                is a set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                equipped with a relation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⋈
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\bowtie B
                between
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B\subseteq X
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical
                notion of a
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proximity+space"} proximity space
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⋈
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
                can be taken as a definition of a set–set apartness space.
            %li
              %p
                A
                %em uniform apartness space
                is a set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                equipped with a collection of “co-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entourages"}> entourages
                ”, each giving a different notion of when two points are apart, satisfying appropriate axioms. In
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complements"} complements
                of the entourages of a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"} uniform space
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniformly+regular"} uniformly regular
          %p
            Since point–point apartness spaces are described at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/apartness+relation"} apartness relation
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proximity+space"} proximity space
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniformly+regular+space"} uniformly regular space
          %h2#pointset_apartness_spaces Point–set apartness spaces
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong apartness space
              is a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              equipped with a relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
              between points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
              and subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\subseteq X
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⋈
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie \emptyset
                for any
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %li
                if
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ⋈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≠
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\neq y
                for all
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\in A
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⋈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie (A\cup B)
                iff
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⋈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie A
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ⋈
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie B
              %li
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ⋈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie A
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ⋈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi z
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi z
                        %mo ⋈
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi z
                        %mo ≠
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \bowtie \{ y \mid \forall z, (z\bowtie A \to z\neq y) \}
          %p
            The relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie A
            should be regarded as a “positive” way of saying that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            does not belong to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure"} closure
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∉
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\notin \overline{A}
          %ol
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\emptyset} = \emptyset
              \.
            %li
              If
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in A
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in \overline{A}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\subseteq \overline{A}
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ∪
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo =
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∪
                        %mi B
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{A} \cup \overline{B} = \overline{A\cup B}
              (and in particular
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mover
                        %mi B
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A\subseteq B) \to (\overline{A}\subseteq \overline{B})
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\subseteq \overline{A}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mover
                        %mi B
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in \overline{B}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in\overline{A}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mover
                          %mi A
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo =
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\overline{A}} = \overline{A}
          %p
            which are precisely the axioms of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            expressed in terms of a closure operator. In constructive mathematics, of course, the law of contraposition does not hold.
          %p
            The axiom
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋈
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie \emptyset
            is almost unnecessary, since the last axiom ensures that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie A
            for any set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            then
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie\emptyset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            (see below) and for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
            there is a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\in X
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\neq y
          %p
            The above definition is almost exactly that of a “pre-apartness” from
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BV11"} BV11
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
            (which category-theoretically is wrong-headed, since it excludes the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is given with an ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inequality+relation"} inequality relation
            that is referred to by the symbol
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≠
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neq
            in axioms 2 and 4. (If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≠
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neq
            is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/denial+inequality"} denial inequality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie A
            then
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∉
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\notin A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie A
            then
            = succeed "\u201D.)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie \{ y \mid \neg(y\bowtie A) \}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            (see below) then this ambient inequality is definable in terms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
            as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie \{y\}
            %a{:href => "#BV11"} BV11
            also require comparability (see below).
          %p
            Axiom 4 is phrased in
            %a{:href => "#BV11"} BV11
            as “if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x, (x\bowtie A \Rightarrow (\forall y\in B, x\neq y))
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x, (x\bowtie A \Rightarrow x\bowtie B)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi z
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo ⋈
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi z
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = \{ y \mid \forall z, (z\bowtie A \to z\neq y) \}
            is the largest set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            satisfying
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x, (x\bowtie A \Rightarrow (\forall y\in B, x\neq y))
          %p
            The earlier paper
            %a{:href => "#BSV02"} BSV02
            omits the axiom
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie \emptyset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            as part of the definition too (see below). An earlier, more predicative presentation of “apartness spaces” can be found in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#FW96"} Waaldijk
          %h2#separation_properties Separation properties
          %p
            Any apartness space comes with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreflexive+relation"} irreflexive relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nleq
            defined by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≰
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \nleq y
            iff
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \bowtie \{y\}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/specialization+order"} specialization order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axioms"} separation axioms
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x\le y) \to (x=y)
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≰
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg(x\nleq y) \to (x=y)
          %p
            We could contrapose this to obtain
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≰
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg(x=y) \to (x\nleq y)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg(x=y)
            with a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/apartness+relation"} apartness relation
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inequality+relation"} inequality relation
            other than the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/denial+inequality"} denial inequality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≰
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x\neq y) \to (x\nleq y)
            that is a purely positive version of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≠
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neq
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tight+relation"} tight
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nleq
            is symmetric (see below) then the negative version of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            says precisely that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nleq
            is tight.
          %p
            Note that axiom 2 implies the converse
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x\bowtie \{y\}) \to (x\neq y)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            property are stated with reference to some ambient inequality
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≠
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neq
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≠
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neq
            can be defined in terms of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
            %em define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≠
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neq
            in this way, then axiom 2 should be stated in terms of the denial inequality (thereby asserting that this relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie \{y\}
            is
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreflexive"} irreflexive
          %p
            If one wants the relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie \{y\}
            to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+relation"} symmetric
            and thus an “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inequality+relation"}> inequality relation
            ” one needs to assert this separately. An apartness space with this property is naturally called
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_0
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                strongly
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_0
            that the specialization order is symmetric (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axioms"} separation axioms
          %p
            However, stating axiom 4 in terms of the
            = succeed "-derived" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \{x,y,z\}
            with the only nonempty apartness relations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie \{z\}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z\bowtie \{x\}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A=\{z\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ⋈
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ y \mid \neg(y\bowtie A)\} = \{y,z\}
            which is not apart from
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            = succeed "-derived" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bowtie
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi u
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⋈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ v \mid \forall u, (u\bowtie A \Rightarrow u \bowtie \{v\})\} = \{z\}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopological+space"} pretopological space
            that is not a topological space; thus only axiom 4 with the denial inequality (or at least a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tight+inequality"} tight inequality
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BV11"} BV11
            = succeed "." do
              %strong reverse Kolmogorov property
          %p
            An apartness space may be called
            %strong comparable
            (nonce definition on this page) if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\bowtie A
            implies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ⋈
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
